    "description": "The Doppler-shift attenuation method was used to measure lifetimes of yrast states in /sup 166/Yb. Three different stopping materials were used and consistent results were obtained over a large range of spins. Values of tau range from 1.20(10) ps at 18/sup +/ to 0.05(1) ps at 34/sup +/. The B(E2) values steadily decrease from 200 to 120 single particle units as the spin increases above 24h-dash-bar. This loss of collectivity is likely to reflect a change toward triaxial shapes. The side-feeding times to these states are longer than the inband feeding times.",
    "title": "Line-shape analysis of high spin states: Collectivity in /sup 166/Yb",
